//! #7605: `--indent 0` prints the newlines and the space after each `:` with no indentation, as jq 1.8
//! does (upstream fix jqlang/jq#3232, "Fix `--indent 0` implicitly enabling `--compact-output`").
//! jq 1.7.1 printed it compactly, as `-c` (#3155 pinned that). The spellings that read as 0 (`-0`,
//! `00`, `+0`) are the same value, and `-c`, `--tab` and `--indent` stay one knob whose last
//! spelling wins: `-c --indent 0` and `--tab --indent 0` print the zero-indent layout, `--indent 0
//! -c` is compact. Expected output was captured from jq 1.8.2 (`/opt/homebrew/bin/jq`) over the
//! generated matrix of spellings, output flags, print routes (the cursor echo, owned values, the
//! `-s`/`-n` eager writer, `--seq`, `--stream`, field access on the streaming fast path) and inputs.
//! The `-C` rows keep jq 1.7.1's colours, which `succinctly jq` follows (#5473): their bytes are jq
//! 1.7.1's `-C --indent 1` output with the one space of indentation removed from each line, which is
//! jq 1.8.2's layout in jq 1.7.1's colours.

